u V^ho + \Gamma^ho{}_{
u\sigma}V^\sigma)$ still contains $(\partial_\mu\Gamma^ho{}_{
u\sigma})V^\sigma$, and derivatives of $\Gamma$ need not vanish at $p$. Swapping and subtracting removes $\partial_\mu\partial_
u V^ho$ and leaves $(\partial_\mu\Gamma^ho{}_{
u\sigma} - \partial_
u\Gamma^ho{}_{\mu\sigma})V^\sigma$. Because the products of Christoffel symbols vanish at $p$, that is $R^ho{}_{\sigma\mu
u}V^\sigma$ there. Both sides are tensors, so the identity then holds in every coordinate system.

